# Fathom — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Fathom carries a small debugging and automation surface, `window.__fathom`, so the
dive can be driven and inspected from code without touching the keyboard or
waiting on real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__fathom` as soon as the game has
initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so it is
present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a read or a pose of the game's state. A pose arranges the maze,
and the game's own sensing, pathfinding, release schedule and contact rules run
from there exactly as they do in play, so a scenario driven from code behaves
exactly like one played by hand.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
